er}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tian972k/micro-fontend-base/commits/29d6b3cf074a0d65fd3d7608a157249cfcd16292/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T12:39:16Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T12:46:12Z","email":"149671057+tian972k@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Tuan Pham"},"message":"docs: render flow diagrams with Mermaid and document Next.js SSR modes\n\n- edge-cases: replace the ASCII MfeHost load sequence with a Mermaid\n  flowchart covering every branch (invalid host, network/404/5xx,\n  maintenance, unmount races, load failure, registration timeout, mount\n  error) colour-coded by outcome.\n- testing-and-quality: CI pipeline as a Mermaid diagram.\n- architecture: new ''Next.js: two delivery modes'' section - the\n  standalone Next.js site is server-rendered (its own SSR deploy), the MFE\n  embedded in the shell is a client-rendered Vite federation bundle; no\n  Vite-based Next runtime is used. Mirrored in creating-a-micro-frontend\n  and edge-cases (MFEs are not SSR''d inside the shell).","tree":{"sha":"e5a915d5474194a3c85372809023853113c1bc68","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tian972k/micro-fontend-base/git/trees/e5a915d5474194a3c85372809023853113c1bc68"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tian972k/micro-fontend-base/git/commits/29d6b3cf074a0d65fd3d7608a157249cfcd16292","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/149671057?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tian972k/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tian972k/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tian972k/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.co