_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tian972k/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tian972k","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tian972k/micro-fontend-base/commits/a49ee7a383f2b69b49cc2ff5ccf98ff26e5933df/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-17T08:27:13Z","email":"phamtuandev0907@gmail.com","name":"tian972k"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T10:13:36Z","email":"149671057+tian972k@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Tuan Pham"},"message":"docs(architecture): add MFE registration/mount and state-sync flow diagrams\n\nTwo new mermaid sequenceDiagrams:\n- MFE Registration & Mount Lifecycle: Shell validates host -> fetch\n  health/manifest -> inject script -> remote registers via\n  AppRegistry -> mfe:registered event -> MountManager.mount runs hooks.\n  Documents the actual current flow, including the event-driven\n  registration and Promise.race timeout fixed earlier.\n- Cross-MFE State Sync Flow: how setState on a shared store singleton\n  relates to the EventBus broadcast via syncStore, and notes that\n  because all MFEs on a page already share one window-singleton store\n  instance, the EventBus sync mainly matters for future cross-tab/\n  cross-window scenarios rather than same-page sync today.","tree":{"sha":"b6c7385ce66368ae465763e141e0237c8ef05d49","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tian972k/micro-fontend-base/git/trees/b6c7385ce66368ae465763e141e0237c8ef05d49"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tian972k/micro-fontend-base/git/commits/a49ee7a383f2b69b49cc2ff5ccf98ff26e5933df","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/149671057?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tian972k/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tian972k/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tian972k/following{/other_user}","