r_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thevladdo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/thevladdo","id":56829605,"login":"thevladdo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2ODI5NjA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thevladdo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thevladdo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thevladdo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thevladdo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thevladdo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thevladdo","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/thevladdo/genui-framework/commits/0197069e4f660e693073a3119bb0e37a67bcbb3f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-26T15:02:56Z","email":"vlad.dogariu@studenti.unicam.it","name":"Vlad Dogariu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-26T15:02:56Z","email":"vlad.dogariu@studenti.unicam.it","name":"Vlad Dogariu"},"message":"Studio turned into a Control Plane\n\nAdds four admin tools over the existing headless backend, each tenant-scoped\nfrom the key and tree-shaken out of the public build. Zone governance moves the\nregistry to two slots per (tenant, zone_id): saving a draft can no longer\noverwrite what production serves, `approve` is the only transition, versions\nspan both slots and a stale write raises a 409. Adds `/api/v1/zone/config`\n(list/get/draft/approve/discard/delete), admin-only `preview_draft` on\n`/zone/render` (always a live bypass, never cached, zeroed by warmup), and a\nper-tenant observed catalog so the console can list zones the site really\nrenders. The audit trail gains a read path (`AuditReader` for the log-pipeline\nsink that answers \"not queryable\" honestly, `FileAuditReader` for JSONL with\nrotated backups, filters and pagination) behind `/api/v1/audit`, and now records\nwhat the guarantee chain removed. The content policy becomes live per-tenant\ndata (`ContentPolicyStore`, `effective_policy` = env plus stored terms, so an\nempty store behaves exactly as before and the global \"*\" stays env-only) behind\n`/api/v1/content-policy`. `/api/v1/whoami` resolves a key to its tenant, and the\nconsole holds one session per tenant with an explicit switcher that remounts the\npage, so a view left on the previous tenant can never write to it.\n\nGives a tenant''s theme a home: `ThemeStore` plus a `TenantTheme` contract that\nmirrors the Playground whitelist token by token, each value pattern-bound so a\nstored theme can restyle a page but never inject CSS, re-checked on read since\nRedis is shared infrastructure. `GET /api/v1/theme` takes a client key (a theme\nis public branding, already visible as CSS custom properties), `PUT` is admin\nand audit-logged. Saving stores config this endpoint serves: the library still\ntakes the theme as a prop, and a host applies the saved one with one fetch at\nboot. The Playground sidebar gains a tenant bar (switch, load, save) and the\nSegment Preview renders with the theme saved for the active tenant. Extracts\n`TenantJsonStore` as the shared tenant-keyed Redis-or-memory store, third\ninstance of the same shape, and moves the content policy store onto it.\n\nExtends the guarantee chain with a redundancy step on both zone paths: the same\nlink target twice in one component loses the repeat, an element with the same\ntarget and wording as an earlier component is removed, and a component emptied\nthat way is dropped whole, all reported in the existing `dropped_components`.\nOne guard instance per render is what lets the streaming path see what the\nvisitor has already been shown. Fixes a real bug behind the same symptom: pinned\npresence was read from bento cards and buttons only, so a pinned link the model\nused as the hero''s single CTA looked missing and came back as a duplicate card.\nPresence is now read from the whole component tree by field name (`is_url_field`\nshared with the URL guard), so it cannot go stale the next time a component type\nlands.","tree":{"sha":"c558060e90c68a782ad89f5f2a6171caaf3f2e8b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/thevladdo/genui-framework/git/trees/c558060e90c68a782ad89f5f2a6171caaf3f2e8b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/thevladdo/genui-framework/git/commits/0197069e4f660e693073a3119bb0e37a67bcbb3f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56829605?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thevladdo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thevladdo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thevladdo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thevladdo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/thevladdo","id":56829605,"login":"thevladdo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2ODI5NjA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thevladdo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thevladdo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thevladdo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thevladdo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thevladdo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thevladdo","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/thevladdo/genui-framework/commit/0197069e4f660e693073a3119bb0e37a67bcbb3f","node_id":"C_kwDOQ5RVXNoAKDAxOTcwNjllNGY2NjBlNjkzMDczYTMxMTliYjBlMzdhNjdiY2JiM2Y","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/thevladdo/genui-framework/commit/2110e47e21f5ea10a8930b1e9fe10a6e2e8fd826","sha":"2110e47e21f5ea10a8930b1e9fe10a6e2e8fd826","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/thevladdo/genui-framework/commits/2110e47e21f5ea10a8930b1e9fe10a6e2e8fd826"}],"sha":"0197069e4f660e693073a3119bb0e37a67bcbb3f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/thevladdo/genui-framework/commits/0197069e4f660e693073a3119bb0e37a67bcbb3f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56829605?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thevladdo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thevladdo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thevladdo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thevladdo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/thevladdo","id":56829605,"login":"thevladdo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2ODI5NjA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thevladdo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thevladdo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thevladdo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thevladdo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thevladdo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thevladdo","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/thevladdo/genui-framework/commits/2110e47e21f5ea10a8930b1e9fe10a6e2e8fd826/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-22T22:30:07Z","email":"vlad.dogariu@studenti.unicam.it","name":"Vlad Dogariu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-22T22:30:07Z","email":"vlad.dogariu@studenti.unicam.it","name":"Vlad Dogariu"},"message":"New components and zone budgeting\n\nIntroduces three new section components (`case_studies`, `quote`, `logo_wall`) across backend schemas/registry/prompts and frontend renderer/types/styles, with full exports and studio preview examples. Adds zone-level component budgeting (`ZONE_MAX_COMPONENTS`, request/registry override, cache-key wiring) and enforces truncation with sanitization reporting on sync and streaming paths. Also expands guards/tests: numeric grounding for case-study metrics, logo/avatar URL image classification, degradation behavior fixes (pricing empty/single-plan detailed fallback, quote avatar attribution rule), and new backend/frontend test suites to pin these contracts.","tree":{"sha":"7453106ec7b2c3840d3f4f07483c353218fa799d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/thevladdo/genui-framework/git/trees/7453106ec7b2c3840d3f4f07483c353218fa799d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/thevladdo/genui-framework/git/commits/2110e47e21f5ea10a8930b1e9fe10a6e2e8fd826","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56829605?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thevladdo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thevladdo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thevladdo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thevladdo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/thevladdo","id":56829605,"login":"thevladdo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2ODI5NjA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thevladdo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thevladdo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thevladdo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thevladdo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thevladdo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thevladdo","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/thevladdo/genui-framework/commit/2110e47e21f5ea10a8930b1e9fe10a6e2e8fd826","node_id":"C_kwDOQ5RVXNoAKDIxMTBlNDdlMjFmNWVhMTBhODkzMGIxZTlmZTEwYTZlMmU4ZmQ4MjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/thevladdo/genui-framework/commit/d2ea91df787abac36fe4eaeebbed914f609b9dc2","sha":"d2ea91df787abac36fe4eaeebbed914f609b9dc2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/thevladdo/genui-framework/commits/d2ea91df787abac36fe4eaeebbed914f609b9dc2"}],"sha":"2110e47e21f5ea10a8930b1e9fe10a6e2e8fd826","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/thevladdo/genui-framework/commits/2110e47e21f5ea10a8930b1e9fe10a6e2e8fd826"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56829605?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thevladdo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thevladdo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thevladdo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thevladdo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/thevladdo","id":56829605,"login":"thevladdo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2ODI5NjA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thevladdo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thevladdo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thevladdo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thevladdo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thevladdo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thevladdo","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/thevladdo/genui-framework/commits/d2ea91df787abac36fe4eaeebbed914f609b9dc2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-22T09:43:15Z","email":"vlad.dogariu@studenti.unicam.it","name":"Vlad Dogariu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-22T09:43:15Z","email":"vlad.dogariu@studenti.unicam.it","name":"Vlad Dogariu"},"message":"Image URL guarding and cap grid columns\n\nSplit URL sanitization into link vs image whitelists so page links can’t be reused as `<img src>`, and add post-sanitize variant downgrades (hero/steps/tabs/content-grid) to keep components coherent when invalid images are stripped. Also cap ContentGrid and StatsBanner columns by item count, extend heading word-wrap coverage, add regression tests for URL/image behavior and grid columns, and improve Studio layout and spacing.","tree":{"sha":"176e7dab25e49ad37b00f33b178a5bfa5fdf9383","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/thevladdo/genui-framework/git/trees/176e7dab25e49ad37b00f33b178a5bfa5fdf9383"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/thevladdo/genui-framework/git/commits/d2ea91df787abac36fe4eaeebbed914f609b9dc2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56829605?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thevladdo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thevladdo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thevladdo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thevladdo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/thevladdo","id":56829605,"login":"thevladdo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2ODI5NjA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thevladdo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thevladdo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thevladdo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thevladdo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thevladdo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thevladdo","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/thevladdo/genui-framework/commit/d2ea91df787abac36fe4eaeebbed914f609b9dc2","node_id":"C_kwDOQ5RVXNoAKGQyZWE5MWRmNzg3YWJhYzM2ZmU0ZWFlZWJiZWQ5MTRmNjA5YjlkYzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/thevladdo/genui-framework/commit/57dbba062edbff8e777aa9a6ced6cc50ea67f701","sha":"57dbba062edbff8e777aa9a6ced6cc50ea67f701","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/thevladdo/genui-framework/commits/57dbba062edbff8e777aa9a6ced6cc50ea67f701"}],"sha":"d2ea91df787abac36fe4eaeebbed914f609b9dc2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/thevladdo/genui-framework/commits/d2ea91df787abac36fe4eaeebbed914f609b9dc2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56829605?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thevladdo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thevladdo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thevladdo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thevladdo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/thevladdo","id":56829605,"login":"thevladdo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2ODI5NjA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thevladdo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thevladdo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thevladdo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thevladdo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thevladdo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thevladdo","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/thevladdo/genui-framework/commits/57dbba062edbff8e777aa9a6ced6cc50ea67f701/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-20T18:19:12Z","email":"vlad.dogariu@studenti.unicam.it","name":"Vlad Dogariu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-20T18:19:12Z","email":"vlad.dogariu@studenti.unicam.it","name":"Vlad Dogariu"},"message":"Watch GenUI do what it was built for: Segment Preview\n\nIntroduces a new local-only Studio Segment Preview tool to test render one zone config across multiple audience profiles, including routing/nav integration, API calls (`/zone/render`, `/health`), segment-key/profile utilities, and dedicated tests.\n\nAlso improves frontend zone rendering with container-query responsiveness, safer bento column sizing (capped by card count), text wrapping and mobile sizing tweaks, and bento caption/text-only styling fixes.\n\nBackend prompt guidance was tightened to keep visible copy as page content (not meta commentary).","tree":{"sha":"2a739adbe9c5a12502c09befc76d8839d63df536","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/thevladdo/genui-framework/git/trees/2a739adbe9c5a12502c09be